Topic: Tools tool descriptions


🛠️ What Are Tools in AI Agents?

Tools are external functions or APIs that the agent can call to perform tasks beyond text generation.

They extend the agent’s abilities — letting it fetch data, control apps, or take real-world actions.

Think of them as the plugins or capabilities the agent can use.


📖 Tool Description:

This description is critical because the agent  uses it to decide which tool to call and how to format the request.

~ What the tool does (purpose).

~ How to call it (parameters, inputs, outputs).

~ When to use it (conditions or triggers).



🚀 Why Tool Descriptions Matter:  

Prevents misuse (agent won’t call the wrong tool).

Makes the agent autonomous (it can pick the right tool without human intervention).

Ensures reliability (structured inputs/outputs).



🧩How the agent uses it:

You ask: “What’s the weather in Delhi right now?”

Agent reads the tool description → sees it needs city.

Agent calls: get_weather(city="Delhi", unit="C").

Tool returns: { "temp": 32, "condition": "Sunny" }.

Agent replies: “It’s 32°C and sunny in Delhi.”


